### Step 3 — Two-phase dynamic validation

#### Pre-check

```bash
if [ ! -f "{{ WORKDIR }}/eval.sh" ]; then
    echo "eval.sh not found — DYNAMIC_SCORE=N/A"
fi
```

#### Phase 1: Revert code_patch (expect FAIL)

```bash
cd {{ WORKDIR }}
git status --short | head -10

if git apply -R /tests/code_patch.diff 2>&1; then
    echo "Revert succeeded"
else
    echo "git apply -R failed, trying file-level revert from base_commit"
    git diff --name-only HEAD | grep -vE 'test_|_test\.|conftest|eval\.sh|setup\.' | \
        xargs -I{} git checkout base_commit -- {} 2>/dev/null || echo "REVERT FAILED"
fi

{% if language == "py" and benchmark != "pro" %}
source /opt/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh 2>/dev/null || source /opt/miniconda3/bin/activate 2>/dev/null || true
conda activate testbed 2>/dev/null || true
{% endif %}
bash {{ WORKDIR }}/eval.sh 2>&1 | tee /tmp/phase1_output.log
echo "Phase 1 exit: $?  (expect non-zero)"
tail -30 /tmp/phase1_output.log
```

#### Phase 2: Restore code_patch (expect PASS)

```bash
find {{ WORKDIR }} -name "*.pyc" -delete 2>/dev/null; find {{ WORKDIR }} -name "__pycache__" -type d -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null
cd {{ WORKDIR }}
git apply /tests/code_patch.diff 2>&1 || git checkout HEAD -- . 2>/dev/null
bash {{ WORKDIR }}/eval.sh 2>&1 | tee /tmp/phase2_output.log
echo "Phase 2 exit: $?  (expect 0)"
tail -30 /tmp/phase2_output.log
```

→ Give **DYNAMIC_SCORE** (0–2 or N/A).

